  "narrative": {
    "storyArc": {
      "hook": {
        "headline": "System Pressure",
        "commentary": "Lead with the KPI band and the six-week trend: waits, LWBS, and boarding have all moved above the operating comfort band together, while arrivals stayed elevated rather than spiking once and falling back.",
        "widgetIds": ["kpi_dtp", "kpi_lwbs", "kpi_boarding", "trend_dtp"],
        "transitionText": "With the enterprise pressure established, move to the sites creating most of the burden."
      },
      "context": {
        "headline": "Where It Is Concentrated",
        "commentary": "The facility ranking and priority table make the problem concrete. Metro Community and North Medical are clearly separated from the stable comparison sites and should be named explicitly in the readout.",
        "widgetIds": ["facility_rank", "priority_table"],
        "transitionText": "Once the sites are clear, explain why the front door is not the whole story."
      },
      "tension": {
        "headline": "What Is Driving It",
        "commentary": "Use the service-line driver view to show that medicine and telemetry discharge friction are amplifying boarding, then use staffing as supporting context rather than the headline explanation.",
        "widgetIds": ["service_line_driver", "staffing_context"],
        "transitionText": "From root cause, step into the downstream consequences already showing up in access and experience."
      },
      "resolution": {
        "headline": "What It Is Causing",
        "commentary": "Patient satisfaction is now sliding in the same facilities where LWBS and diversion kept worsening. This turns the throughput issue from an operational nuisance into a patient-facing leadership problem.",
        "widgetIds": ["experience_consequence"],
        "transitionText": "Close with the specific operating actions the room should prioritize this week."
      },
      "callToAction": {
        "headline": "What We Do Next",
        "commentary": "Focus discharge flow, telemetry bed release, and evening surge coverage at Metro Community and North Medical this week. The ask is narrow on purpose: a few site-specific operating levers should relieve the largest portion of the burden first.",
        "widgetIds": ["priority_table", "service_line_driver", "staffing_context"],
        "transitionText": "End by reinforcing that this is a reusable dashboard artifact, not a one-time workshop screenshot."
      }
    },
    "executiveSummary": "ED throughput pressure has persisted for six weeks, Metro Community and North Medical now drive most of the delay, inpatient flow is the main amplifier, and action this week should target discharge throughput, telemetry release, and evening surge coverage.",
    "presenterNotes": [
      "1. System Pressure: open with the risk trio of Door To Provider, LWBS Rate, and Avg Boarding Hours, then use the six-week line to prove persistence.",
      "2. Where It Is Concentrated: move immediately to facility accountability and name Metro Community and North Medical before reading additional numbers.",
      "3. What Is Driving It: explain that medicine and telemetry discharge flow are the primary drivers, with staffing strain as a secondary amplifier on evening and night shifts.",
      "4. What It Is Causing: connect the satisfaction slide to the earlier throughput and diversion movement rather than presenting experience as an isolated quality issue.",
      "5. What We Do Next: close on a bounded operating response and note that the same DashboardSpec can remain mock-backed or later move selected views toward the existing live or hybrid path."
    ]
  },
